1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,279
This is the Copilot settings blade.

2
00:00:02,279 --> 00:00:05,240
One entry, screen and camera sharing.

3
00:00:06,210 --> 00:00:08,650
It opens into two controls, not one.

4
00:00:09,604 --> 00:00:10,404
Screens.

5
00:00:10,404 --> 00:00:11,404
Cameras.

6
00:00:11,404 --> 00:00:14,124
One row, two values behind it.

7
00:00:15,086 --> 00:00:19,286
Screens offers all users, no users, or specific groups.

8
00:00:20,486 --> 00:00:21,566
So does Cameras.

9
00:00:21,566 --> 00:00:22,646
Independently.

10
00:00:25,116 --> 00:00:28,395
Nothing was changed to film this, which is why Save is greyed.

11
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:33,850
Turn screens off and you have done half the job.

12
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:36,610
The camera is still on, and your note says handled.

13
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,780
An audit note that records one value carries neither.

14
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:46,020
Write down two, one per control, and check Save is greyed before you record either.

